	"responsive": {
		"strategy": "A stack of full-bleed marketing bands — hero, a card row, a customer-logo strip — the same basic shape as Apple's homepage. But where Apple eventually caps and centres its content on a big screen, Webflow never does: the scan measures the hero band at essentially the full browser width at 1280, 1920 AND 3440 alike, with no growing side margin. The one place width actually bites is the six-card highlight row, which does not wrap: the last card is visibly clipped at the browser edge at 1280 and only shows whole once the window is wide enough. Below about 480-991px the nav collapses to a hamburger and the page becomes one column.",
